format: meaning/draft-1
id: ecb-daily
name: ECB daily euro foreign exchange reference quotes
description: >-
  Authored preparatory meanings for the native time, currency and rate strings
  extracted from the ECB daily XML resource. EUR is explicit base context;
  this metadata adds no EUR row, publication instant, historical lookup,
  reciprocal or cross-rate. Source activation and paid applicability are blocked.
license: CC0-1.0
models:
  ecb: ecb-daily.modelspec.hcl
sources:
  - id: ecb-daily
    provider: European Central Bank
    dataset: Euro foreign exchange reference rates daily XML
    url: https://www.ecb.europa.eu/stats/eurofxref/eurofxref-daily.xml
    note: >-
      Source rates are subject to ECB reuse conditions at
      https://www.ecb.europa.eu/services/using-our-site/disclaimer/html/index.en.html.
      CC0 applies only to authored meaning/model metadata, not rates or ECB
      documents. No source rows, XML, snapshot or terms body are retained here.
concepts:
  - id: ecb-fx-reference-quote
    kind: entity
    extends: meaning://github.com/meaninggraph/core/fx-reference-quote?ref=1de4de09a449b9978a6155f226669e02986cb7d9
    labels:
      en: ECB daily reference quote
    description: >-
      One quote currency on one returned reference date under ECB methodology,
      directed as quote-currency units per one EUR. The pair (time, currency)
      is unique within one response, not an immutable cross-read identity or
      supported point-read key. The adapter's currency locator is scoped to
      that transient response. Publication may be amended; a read observation
      identity distinguishes consumed responses. Registration admits no execution.
    source: ecb-daily
    bindings:
      - model: modelspec:///ecb.FxReferenceQuote
        role: entity
  - id: ecb-reference-date
    kind: attribute
    of: ecb-fx-reference-quote
    extends: meaning://github.com/meaninggraph/core/fx-reference-date?ref=1de4de09a449b9978a6155f226669e02986cb7d9
    labels:
      en: ECB reference date
    description: >-
      Native Cube.time as a validated Gregorian YYYY-MM-DD calendar date,
      without a time zone or midnight timestamp. Neither publication nor fetch
      time. A different requested date is unavailable, not the latest day.
    bindings:
      - model: modelspec:///ecb.FxReferenceQuote
        property: time
        role: value
  - id: ecb-base-currency
    kind: attribute
    of: ecb-fx-reference-quote
    extends: meaning://github.com/meaninggraph/core/fx-base-currency?ref=1de4de09a449b9978a6155f226669e02986cb7d9
    labels:
      en: ECB base currency
    description: >-
      EUR is a constant of this source definition and quote direction. It is
      not a native row field, not a quote of rate one and has no field binding.
  - id: ecb-quote-currency
    kind: attribute
    of: ecb-fx-reference-quote
    extends: meaning://github.com/meaninggraph/core/fx-quote-currency?ref=1de4de09a449b9978a6155f226669e02986cb7d9
    labels:
      en: ECB quote currency
    description: >-
      Native uppercase currency code in the returned daily publication, naming
      a currency. No country, tender interval, successor or transaction role
      is inferred. The core currency starter values are not a complete ECB
      code allowlist. An absent quote stays unavailable, never zero or one.
    bindings:
      - model: modelspec:///ecb.FxReferenceQuote
        property: currency
        role: value
        note: Native code; no complete core-value coverage or country-identity claim.
  - id: ecb-indicative-reference-rate
    kind: attribute
    of: ecb-fx-reference-quote
    extends: meaning://github.com/meaninggraph/core/indicative-fx-reference-rate?ref=1de4de09a449b9978a6155f226669e02986cb7d9
    labels:
      en: ECB indicative reference rate
    description: >-
      Native positive decimal lexical string of quote-currency units per one
      EUR, with every supplied digit and trailing zero preserved. No binary
      float, fixed scale, reciprocal, cross-rate, conversion, daily average,
      closing or transaction-price equivalence. Exact-decimal transformations
      need separate admission and rounding/notice evidence. ECB rates are for
      information; the ECB discourages transaction use.
    bindings:
      - model: modelspec:///ecb.FxReferenceQuote
        property: rate
        role: value
